{
  "about": "M4: value of information of an analog test before flight (plan 7.3, model 4).\n\nTree: fly as is, or test first and redesign if the test fails. L = loss if a terrain defect ends\nthe mission, R = redesign and delay cost, p = prior probability of the defect, s = sensitivity\n(the test finds a real defect), c = specificity (no false alarm). A redesign removes the defect.\n\n  no information:     E0   = min(p L, R)                 (fly as is, or always redesign)\n  perfect information: EVPI = E0 - p min(L, R)\n  one analog test:    P+ = s p + (1 - c)(1 - p);  p+ = s p / P+;  p- = (1 - s) p / (1 - P+)\n                      E1 = P+ min(p+ L, R) + (1 - P+) min(p- L, R)\n                      EVSI = E0 - E1   (0 <= EVSI <= EVPI)\n  net value = EVSI - campaign cost (M1, converted to USD)\n\nL per mass class = Moon delivery cost (M6, P50) + published hardware cost where one exists (VIPER\nproject cost, OIG, January 2024). R = fraction of L. p, s, c and the fraction are ILLUSTRATIVE.\nCan claim: the value rises with fidelity and never exceeds EVPI; the order of magnitude against a\ncampaign cost. Cannot claim: anything measured; linking site similarity to s is an assumption.",
  "units": "USD (nominal; Moon side in USD because its sources are USD)",
